    <div class="staff-member__bio">
      <h2 class="staff-member__name">Jim Stephens</h2>
      <p class="staff-member__role">Music Director</p>

      <p>Jim and Priscilla Stephens enjoy the ministry at Faith. The church ministry has been a blessing to us.</p>

      <p>I am a native South Carolinian and grew up in a pastor&rsquo;s home. Priscilla grew up in Bolivia, South America. Her parents were missionaries. We met while students at Tennessee Temple University and were married in 1972. We have three children, all graduates of Christian colleges and are serving the Lord. We have &ldquo;no greater joy than to hear that our children walk in truth&rdquo;. And, we enjoy our 14 grandchildren.</p>

      <p>I had the distinct privilege of serving our country in the US Army from 1967&ndash;1970 as a paratrooper with the 101st Airborne Division in Vietnam and the 82nd Airborne Division stateside. I am grateful for our great country.</p>

      <p>We were involved in Christian Education for 30 plus years and also have served on the church staff of churches in Tennessee, North Carolina, and South Carolina. We were also the directors for a camp for &ldquo;at-risk-teens&rdquo; for 5 years. During that time we were able to reach many teens for Christ. We moved to Raymore to help with the homeschooling for our grandchildren.</p>

      <p>Our mission continues to be Jude 22 &mdash; &ldquo;making a difference&rdquo; in the lives of people.</p>

